{"name":"Wonton Dumpling","hex":"#d0a46d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wonton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Chinese dumpling, often stuffed with varieties of meat or seafood and vegetables."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonton"},{"term":"dumpling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball of dough that is cooked and may have a filling and/or additional ingredients in the dough. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n Specifically, a ball of dough used in stews and other sauced dishes; a thick noodle.\n Specifically, a food composed of a dough wrapper around a filling.","Specifically, a ball of dough used in stews and other sauced dishes; a thick noodle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumpling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wonton","blocks":[{"text":"A wonton is a type of Chinese dumpling commonly found across regional styles of Chinese cuisine. It is also spelled wantan or wuntun, a transliteration from Cantonese wan4 tan1, and wenden from Shanghainese hhun den. Even though there are many different styles of wonton served throughout China, Cantonese wontons are the most popular in the West due to the predominance of Cantonese restaurants overseas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Pork_Steamed_Wontons.jpg/330px-Pork_Steamed_Wontons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonton"},{"title":"Dumpling","blocks":[{"text":"Dumplings are a broad class of dishes that consist of pieces of cooked dough, often wrapped around a filling. The dough can be based on bread, wheat or other flours, or potatoes, and it may be filled with meat, fish, tofu, cheese, vegetables, or a combination. Dumplings may be prepared using a variety of cooking methods and are found in many world cuisines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/HK_SYP_%E8%A5%BF%E7%87%9F%